    {
      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "Test cleanup removes a hardcoded \"alias\" IDP instead of the IDP it created",
      "description": "In the creation loop, each provider is created as `\"idp-alias-\" + i`, but the cleanup registration is `getCleanup().addCleanup(testRealm().identityProviders().get(\"alias\")::remove);`. The `get(\"alias\")` call is evaluated when `addCleanup` runs, so the cleanup targets a nonexistent IDP named `\"alias\"`. The 20 IDPs created by the loop are never removed. The same mistake appears again after the `idp-alias-20` creation near the step 1 block. Cleanup should bind to the alias that was actually created, for example `getCleanup().addCleanup(testRealm().identityProviders().get(\"idp-alias-\" + i)::remove)`, with the equivalent fix for `idp-alias-20`.",
